From: fexdroid
Subject: [PATCH] Core: TSO off in valid ranges also for blocks with no volatile instruction

ExtendedVolatileMetadata with only a module name ("disable TSO for a full
module") had no effect: the override was set only for blocks that contain an
instruction listed as needing TSO, and such a module lists none.

Local patch, not upstream (NOTES.md N-041).
---
diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
index 8286c14..cf073ce 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
@@ -579,9 +579,11 @@ ContextImpl::GenerateIR(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState* Thread, uint64_t Gue
       bool BlockInForceTSOValidRange = false;
       auto InstForceTSOIt = ForceTSOInstructions.end();
       if (ForceTSOValidRanges.Contains({Block.Entry, Block.Entry + Block.Size})) {
+        // fexdroid: a block in a valid range with no instruction that needs TSO is the common case
+        // (a module listed by name only has none at all) and is the one that must run without TSO.
+        BlockInForceTSOValidRange = true;
         if (auto It = ForceTSOInstructions.lower_bound(Block.Entry); It != ForceTSOInstructions.end() && *It < Block.Entry + Block.Size) {
           InstForceTSOIt = It;
-          BlockInForceTSOValidRange = true;
         }
       }
 
